Generally, bones files are not even compatible across binaries for the same
platform. Especially if you want to change certian options.

I do remember someone posting that they made a Linux binary that is
bones-compatible with the official Windows distribution though, so it
looks like it's possible. Search the archives for the required
configuration (I imagine the post contains the switch mms-bitfields so
you may use it as a keyword).

Of course, you can just as easily compile NetHack for Windows using
the free MinGW compiler.

